# A false assert that is an all over an extractor prints the values the all
# found false, each with its place, and counts the rest; --all-values adds
# every value. JUnit carries the same message. The verdict and the exit code
# are the same either way. SARIF puts the result at the first value the
# message shows and links every other value; any other false assert stays
# at the first value.
! exec errata check -c addresses.yaml
cmp stdout offenders.txt

! exec errata check -c addresses.yaml --all-values
cmp stdout every.txt

! exec errata check -c addresses.yaml -f junit
stdout 'message="assert: the expression is false&#xA;  expression: addresses.all\(a, a.endsWith\(&#39;@example.org&#39;\)\)&#xA;  the all is false for 1 of the 3 values of addresses:&#xA;  addresses\[1\] = &#34;kim@gmail.com&#34; at users.py:2&#xA;  2 more values not shown: errata check --all-values prints every value"'

! exec errata check -c addresses.yaml -f sarif
stdout '"locations": \[\s*\{\s*"physicalLocation": \{\s*"artifactLocation": \{\s*"uri": "users.py",\s*"uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"\s*\},\s*"region": \{\s*"startLine": 2\s*\}'
stdout '"startLine": 1\s*\}\s*\},\s*"message": \{\s*"text": "\\"alice@example.org\\" \(addresses\)"'
stdout '"startLine": 3\s*\}\s*\},\s*"message": \{\s*"text": "\\"sam@example.org\\" \(addresses\)"'

! exec errata check -c exists.yaml -f sarif
stdout '"locations": \[\s*\{\s*"physicalLocation": \{\s*"artifactLocation": \{\s*"uri": "users.py",\s*"uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"\s*\},\s*"region": \{\s*"startLine": 1\s*\}'

-- exists.yaml --
checks:
  - id: some-address-is-kim
    reason: The fixture names kim at the reserved domain.
    scope: repo
    extract:
      addresses: {regex: {file: users.py, pattern: '([a-z]+@[a-z.]+)'}}
    assert: addresses.exists(a, a == 'kim@example.org')
-- addresses.yaml --
checks:
  - id: reserved-addresses
    reason: A fixture address outside reserved space reads as a real mailbox.
    scope: repo
    extract:
      addresses: {regex: {file: users.py, pattern: '([a-z]+@[a-z.]+)'}}
    assert: addresses.all(a, a.endsWith('@example.org'))
-- users.py --
ALICE = "alice@example.org"
KIM = "kim@gmail.com"
SAM = "sam@example.org"
-- offenders.txt --
FALSE reserved-addresses (repo)
  why:  A fixture address outside reserved space reads as a real mailbox.
  said: assert: the expression is false
          expression: addresses.all(a, a.endsWith('@example.org'))
          the all is false for 1 of the 3 values of addresses:
          addresses[1] = "kim@gmail.com" at users.py:2
          2 more values not shown: errata check --all-values prints every value

1 erratum, 0 unknown. Coverage: ran 1, skipped 0.
-- every.txt --
FALSE reserved-addresses (repo)
  why:  A fixture address outside reserved space reads as a real mailbox.
  said: assert: the expression is false
          expression: addresses.all(a, a.endsWith('@example.org'))
          the all is false for 1 of the 3 values of addresses:
          addresses[1] = "kim@gmail.com" at users.py:2
          every value:
          addresses[0] = "alice@example.org" at users.py:1
          addresses[1] = "kim@gmail.com" at users.py:2
          addresses[2] = "sam@example.org" at users.py:3

1 erratum, 0 unknown. Coverage: ran 1, skipped 0.
